meta {
  name: Customer_Cart
  seq: 15
}

auth {
  mode: apikey
}

auth:apikey {
  key: X-Customer-Auth-Token
  value: {{customerToken}}
  placement: header
}

docs {
  Requests of a signed-in customer: the customer token goes to `X-Customer-Auth-Token`. Get it with `Customer_Auth` sign-in or confirm. A guest token (`Customer_Auth / guest`) opens only `Show the cart` and the item requests.

  Scenario, in `seq` order (runtime variables are saved by the requests):
  
  1. `Add an item to the cart` — `productVariationId` of the environment → `cartItemId`.
  2. `Show the cart`, `Update a cart item` — prices, stock (`available_quantity`), quantity.
  3. `Choose the address` — `addressId` from `Customer_Account / Add an address` → `packageId`, `pickUpDeliveryMethodId`.
  4. `List delivery options` for the chosen address.
  5. `Show the checkout` — packages, methods, payment, `deliverable`.
  6. `List pick-up points` → `pickUpPointId`; `Choose the delivery and the pick-up point`.
  7. `Apply a promo code` — `promo_code`, `promo_discount` and the discounted `total` come in the checkout; `Remove the promo code` drops it. `SALE10` is an example: put a code of your site.
  8. `Customer_Order / Place the order`. `Remove items from the cart` empties the cart: skip it when you go on to `Customer_Order`.
}
